# AESOPUS computation completed
#  Calculations performed with AESOPUS 2.0
#  Tables of Rosseland mean opacities
#  Reference papers: Marigo & Aringer 2009 (A&A, 508, 1539); Marigo et al. 2022 (ApJ 940, 129), 2023 with solid grains
#
#  Definitions:
#  The base-10 logarithm of the Rosseland mean opacity [cm**2/g] as a function
#  of log10(T) for columns of constant log10(R), where:
#  R=density[g/cm**3]/T6**3, T6=1.e-6*T[K]
#
#  Ranges of state parameters
#
#  log10(T) range: nt= 129  values from  4.500  to  2.580
#  log10(T) = [2.580,3.700] in steps of  0.010
#  log10(T) = ]3.700,4.500] in steps of  0.050
#
#  log10(R) range: nre= 19  values from -8.000  to  1.000
#                           in steps of  0.500
#
#
#  Composition parameters:
#
#       X     = hydrogen mass fraction
#               mh =  1 values from 0.200 to 0.200 in steps of 0.100
#       Zref  = 4.000000E-03  reference metallicity
#       Z     = actual metallicity
#
#       Reference solar mixture: Asplund et al. 2021 A&A 653 A141 ---- Zsun =  0.01389  (C/O)sun =  0.58898
#
